From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:25:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hsl/hwb none serialization form + lab-family
 keyword-none-as-zero

Two Blink behaviors that WPT exposed:

- None-carrying hsl()/hwb() computed values serialize s/l (w/b) with
  '%' only when directly authored; relative-origin and color-mix
  results use plain numbers. A new HSL_HWB_AS_PERCENT color flag is set
  by the no-origin resolve path and stripped from mix results.
- Bare channel keywords referencing a none origin channel yield 0 in
  the lab(), lch(), oklab(), oklch() and color() families (the WPT file
  carries a 'FIXME: Clarify with spec editors' for exactly this); rgb,
  hsl and hwb keep carrying none forward. Literal none is untouched.

Also fold zero-sum color-mix pairwise at 50/50 per fold instead of
equal 1/n weights, so 3-item all-zero mixes match Chrome's expected
color(srgb 0.25 0.12549 0.5 / 0) shape.
---
 color/color_function.rs | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 color/component.rs      | 15 +++++++++++++++
 color/mix.rs            | 17 ++++++++---------
 color/mod.rs            |  2 ++
 color/to_css.rs         |  6 +++++-
 5 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

